mass spectrometry dataset acquired on a quadrupole selecting, quadrupole collision cell, time-of-flight mass spectrometer: I. How much of the data is theoretically interpretable by search engines?</article-title><source>Mol Cell Proteomics</source><year>2005</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>1189</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15923566</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baldwin</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Protein Identification by Mass Spectrometry</article-title><source>Molecular &#x00026; Cellular Proteomics</source><year>2004</year><volume>3.1</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14608001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Xia</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Meila</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hackett</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of the stochastic variation in LTQ single scan mass spectra</article-title><source>Rapid Commun Mass Spectrom</source><year>2006</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>1551</fpage><lpage>1557</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16628562</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Na</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Paek</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quality assessment of tandem mass spectra based on cumulative intensity normalization</article-title><source>J Proteome Res</source><year>2006</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>3241</fpage><lpage>3248</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17137325<